  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>H</mi></math> curve for a ferromagnet is shown in the figure. The ferromagnet is placed inside a long solenoid with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>turns</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The current that should be passed in the solenoid to demagnetize the ferromagnet completely is,&nbsp;<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d27b2bb6-aec7-41d8-95e0-32c2c19d0832-image.png\" style=\"width: 295px; height: 250px;\" /></p>",
